Prefix: : <https://finsight-tech.com/ontology/examples/economic-and-analytical-meaning#>
Prefix: xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>

Ontology: <https://finsight-tech.com/ontology/examples/economic-and-analytical-meaning>


# ************************************************************************
# Economic Situation, Observation and Analytical Meaning
# ************************************************************************
#
# Provides a panoramic model of what may appear after a trade: positions,
# obligations, payments, observations and analytical results. The file keeps
# these concepts distinct without trying to solve each modelling problem yet.
#

Datatype: xsd:dateTime
Datatype: xsd:decimal


### Core financial concepts

Class: Portfolio

Class: Security

Class: Trade

# Position is intentionally shallow here. The next modelling problem will
# examine whether a position is a continuing thing, a relationship, an
# aggregation, an observation or some combination of these ideas.

Class: Position


### Economic relationships

ObjectProperty: heldBy
    Domain: Position
    Range: Portfolio

ObjectProperty: positionIn
    Domain: Position
    Range: Security


### Obligations and actual payment

Class: PaymentObligation

Class: BusinessEvent

Class: Payment
    SubClassOf: BusinessEvent

ObjectProperty: appliedTo
    Domain: Payment
    Range: PaymentObligation


### Observations

Class: Observation

Class: PositionObservation
    SubClassOf: Observation

ObjectProperty: observesPosition
    Domain: PositionObservation
    Range: Position

DataProperty: observedQuantity
    Domain: PositionObservation
    Range: xsd:decimal

DataProperty: observedAt
    Domain: Observation
    Range: xsd:dateTime


### Analytical measurements

Class: AnalyticalMeasurement

Class: ValuationMeasurement
    SubClassOf: AnalyticalMeasurement

Class: PnLMeasurement
    SubClassOf: AnalyticalMeasurement

Class: RiskMeasurement
    SubClassOf: AnalyticalMeasurement


### Analytical results

Class: AnalyticalResult

Class: ValuationResult
    SubClassOf: AnalyticalResult

Class: PnLResult
    SubClassOf: AnalyticalResult

Class: RiskResult
    SubClassOf: AnalyticalResult

DataProperty: resultAmount
    Domain: AnalyticalResult
    Range: xsd:decimal


### Measurement subjects and results

ObjectProperty: analysesPosition
    Domain: AnalyticalMeasurement
    Range: Position

ObjectProperty: analysesPortfolio
    Domain: AnalyticalMeasurement
    Range: Portfolio

ObjectProperty: produces
    Domain: AnalyticalMeasurement
    Range: AnalyticalResult

Class: PositionValuation
    SubClassOf:
        ValuationMeasurement,
        analysesPosition exactly 1 Position,
        produces some ValuationResult

Class: PositionPnLMeasurement
    SubClassOf:
        PnLMeasurement,
        analysesPosition exactly 1 Position,
        produces some PnLResult

Class: PortfolioRiskMeasurement
    SubClassOf:
        RiskMeasurement,
        analysesPortfolio exactly 1 Portfolio,
        produces some RiskResult


### Analytical inputs and methods

Class: AnalyticalInput

Class: MarketObservation
    SubClassOf:
        Observation,
        AnalyticalInput

Class: ValuationMethod

Class: RiskMethod

ObjectProperty: usesInput
    Domain: AnalyticalMeasurement
    Range: AnalyticalInput

ObjectProperty: usesValuationMethod
    Domain: ValuationMeasurement
    Range: ValuationMethod

ObjectProperty: usesRiskMethod
    Domain: RiskMeasurement
    Range: RiskMethod


### Scenario context

Class: Scenario

ObjectProperty: underScenario
    Domain: AnalyticalMeasurement
    Range: Scenario

# A Scenario represents hypothetical analytical context. It is not an
# observation that the assumed market movement actually occurred.

